A||||5||Tweek||Question about oem wings||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||05-05-2001||09:24 PM||||I got a wing of a notchback fiero the other day... It was a 2.5l and the wing was not stock equipment on the particualr car. My question is..  are all the stock wings the same? this one is one piece including the mounts, but some people indicate that the mounts are separate...||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||05-05-2001||10:52 PM||||If the wing stanchions are not separate pieces from the wing itself, then it's not an OEM wing - it's an aftermarket wing.<P>All OEM wings have separate stanchions screwed to the underside - none of the OEM versions had molded-in stanchions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||05-05-2001||11:49 PM||||...Unless the previous owner 'glassed it over. Makes it look better IMO. Does it look the same as a stock wing?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tweek||05-06-2001||11:51 AM||||It doesnt look like anything was glassed in. So it probably is an aftermarket one, at least they did a good job in making it look like an oem wing. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||05-06-2001||12:56 PM||||OR it could be something else like a Firebird spoiler. They are lower profile and flat. All one piece.. I have one on my 88 T-top coupe...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tweek||05-06-2001||04:34 PM||||Well, I did see a firebird wing as well, it wasnt quite the same. The one does have that small lip at the back, When I get home I'll take some pictures and post em. Either way, I think I got a good deal for $25.||||reg||1
